{"kind":"request","text":"Please review draft 7 of notes/2026-10-19-sales-applications-design.md at 27f236d6eb0d88fe274cdedef5cae9bb1d96f85d on planner/sales-applications-20261019 (request 7f569087, promise 28988cd9; replaces ae3b059c). One Markdown path on main 2127d5c5. It answers 79613e7c. F2: intake no longer creates approvals; the owner opens the price approval and the terms approval as one item each once their requirements exist (open-price-approval, open-terms-approval under bid.own, refused approval-exists), bound to the requirement they cover; assemble is guarded on the bid's single import being confirmed (impossible while a mapping is proposed), every row of it reviewed or declined with a reason, both approval items present and granted at the current revisions they cover, and a rendering at those revisions; the all-row and immutable-assembly prose is preserved (5.2, 5.3). F3: no member writes the publication state; the submit and publish sends declare a result clause, as the lending library's publish act does, whose effects write the submission's or post's state and the destination's binding (sending scope and incarnation, source fact, send ordinal, path, content digest) with the destination as the authenticated sender; confirmed only when all of them equal the expected values, refused with the result's reason, superseded on a superseding result, unknown left as is and not resent; no act has an effect on those slots; a member's reading of the public receipt file is their statement, shown with their name, never confirmed; record-publication is gone (5.2, 5.3, 6.2, 6.3). F5: the bound is per bid room, not per file: one import (a second refused import-exists), at most one hundred requirements (open-requirement refused bid-full), texts at most four thousand characters and an import's texts under 128 KiB, refused by name at import before any requirement opens; a changed spreadsheet is a new bid room with the old one withdrawn and referenced, a small correction is a remap; larger matrices deferred (5.2, 5.3, 5.4, 8). C3's done-when now exercises the second import, an oversized cell, a missing approval and a result whose binding differs. Draft 6 reframed section 2 as 'Why coordinating is easier', with the authority, attribution and replay properties stated as the floor; it is a design argument, not a claim that anything is built. Documentation only; no gate.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3262966030bbba05a6413e5afd00e993a8e216bf","branch":"planner/sales-applications-20261019","conditions":"exact-head design review of 27f236d6 with architecture, security and simplification conclusions; 79613e7c F2, F3 and F5 answered; the definitions fit the landed forms; claims about what exists today are accurate; links resolve; plain English, no product names","head":"27f236d6eb0d88fe274cdedef5cae9bb1d96f85d","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"4817b532e7a1a118634cb7947b05f7d5d16f726c9d30ea22ff7eaf7db3634e80"}}